\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces This figure describes three stylized theoretical processes consistent with an observed Black-White gap in outcomes. Solid red arrows denote a harmful ($-$) effect of segregation; solid blue arrows denote a beneficial ($+$) effect; the dashed gray arrow denotes a null effect. Only Panel (B) implies a strict zero-sum transfer of advantage from Black to White residents; Panels (A) and (C) generate the same qualitative inequality without any White benefit.}}{5}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:zero-sum-processes}{{1}{5}{This figure describes three stylized theoretical processes consistent with an observed Black-White gap in outcomes. Solid red arrows denote a harmful ($-$) effect of segregation; solid blue arrows denote a beneficial ($+$) effect; the dashed gray arrow denotes a null effect. Only Panel (B) implies a strict zero-sum transfer of advantage from Black to White residents; Panels (A) and (C) generate the same qualitative inequality without any White benefit}{figure.1}{}}
